# Task 2 – Basic `chown` Operations

## Create a File

```bash id="o1qt10"
touch devops-file.txt
```

## Check Current Owner

```bash id="1hiviv"
ls -l devops-file.txt
```

---

## Change Owner to `tokyo`

```bash id="d5o5me"
sudo chown tokyo devops-file.txt
```

### Verify

```bash id="whcy45"
ls -l devops-file.txt
```

---

## Change Owner to `berlin`

```bash id="5ee01g"
sudo chown berlin devops-file.txt
```

### Verify

```bash id="91d45z"
ls -l devops-file.txt
```

### Observation

The file ownership was successfully changed first to **tokyo** and then to **berlin**.

### Key Learning

```bash id="v4jdqa"
chown <owner> <file>
```

changes the user owner of a file.

