# Task 3 – Basic `chgrp` Operations

## Create File

```bash id="nd7b39"
touch team-notes.txt
```

## Check Current Group

```bash id="d6o7b0"
ls -l team-notes.txt
```

---

## Create Group

```bash id="f7t7p5"
sudo groupadd money-heist
```

## Change Group Ownership

```bash id="f0b3zq"
sudo chgrp money-heist team-notes.txt
```

## Verify

```bash id="49f5w2"
ls -l team-notes.txt
```

### Observation

The group ownership was successfully changed to **money-heist**.

### Key Learning

```bash id="x7k1fu"
chgrp <group> <file>
```

changes the group owner of a file or directory.

