# Task 5 – Recursive Ownership

## Create Directory Structure

```bash id="vrz5lu"
mkdir -p heist-project/vault
mkdir -p heist-project/plans

touch heist-project/vault/gold.txt
touch heist-project/plans/strategy.conf
```

## Create Group

```bash id="z86m0q"
sudo groupadd planners
```

## Change Ownership Recursively

```bash id="q44z2t"
sudo chown -R professor:planners heist-project
```

### What `-R` Means

The `-R` option means **recursive**.

It applies the ownership change to:

```text id="8izd8k"
heist-project
     |
     +── vault
     |     └── gold.txt
     |
     +── plans
           └── strategy.conf
```

### Verify

```bash id="n6j7o2"
ls -lR heist-project
```

### Observation

The ownership of `heist-project` and its contents was changed to:

```text id="hnj0in"
Owner → professor
Group → planners
```

