# Ownership Quick Reference

| Command                         | Purpose                                |
| ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| `ls -l`                         | Display file ownership and permissions |
| `chown user file`               | Change the user owner                  |
| `chgrp group file`              | Change the group owner                 |
| `chown user:group file`         | Change both owner and group            |
| `chown -R user:group directory` | Change ownership recursively           |

### Easy Way to Remember

```text id="3g9lqg"
chown → Change Owner
chgrp → Change Group
```

