# Real-World DevOps Connection

File ownership is important when managing:

```text id="5w6t8f"
Application directories
        ↓
/opt/app

Web content
        ↓
/var/www

Configuration files
        ↓
/etc

Log directories
        ↓
/var/log
```

For example, an application directory may need to be owned by a specific service account:

```bash id="q4h2y7"
sudo chown -R appuser:appgroup /opt/myapp
```

This allows the application to access the files while maintaining controlled permissions.

