# Troubleshooting Example

### Problem

An application reports:

```text id="u7ojxu"
Permission denied
```

### Step 1 – Check Ownership and Permissions

```bash id="3w4q4s"
ls -l /opt/myapp
```

### Step 2 – Check the User Running the Application

```bash id="0h3plp"
ps -ef | grep myapp
```

### Step 3 – Check User and Group Membership

```bash id="0knu1k"
id <username>
```

### Step 4 – Correct Ownership if Required

```bash id="3u4qhe"
sudo chown -R appuser:appgroup /opt/myapp
```

### Step 5 – Verify

```bash id="ny7y2t"
ls -l /opt/myapp
```

### Troubleshooting Flow

```text id="yrx1ul"
Permission Denied
      ↓
Check Owner
      ↓
Check Group
      ↓
Check Permissions
      ↓
Check Application User
      ↓
Correct Ownership/Permissions
      ↓
Test Again
```

